build/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
managed_components/
.vscode/
.idea/
# Local-only LAN prototype credentials; never publish credential-bearing binaries.
main/av_private_config.h
build-av/
build-demo/
# Any other build directory. A local build directory was added here by name once
# and the next one -- created with a different name, for a public build -- was
# not covered. Its .elf happened to be clean only because a public build omits
# the private header; that is luck, not a rule, and the rule has to hold for
# whatever directory someone happens to build into.
build-*/
__pycache__/
# No firmware image belongs in the repository: the AV prototype build compiles the
# private header into it, so an image carries the WiFi credentials and the pairing
# token. Searching an image for those strings does not show them -- the compiler
# inlines short literals as instruction immediates -- so "I looked and did not
# find them" is not evidence that an image is clean. Blocks the firmware by name
# as well as by extension, so one copied to an unexpected directory is still out.
FoloToy-AI-Passport*.bin
*.bin
# The debug information in an ELF carries string literals that the compiled image
# does not: a local build's .elf contains the WiFi password and the pairing token
# in full, readable with a plain text search, while the same build's .bin does
# not. Anything that carries debug info has to stay out for that reason.
*.elf
*.map
# ...except the generated glyph table, which the build needs and which holds no
# secrets. Must follow the blanket rule above to be re-included.
!main/ui_font_cjk.bin

# ...and the copy the flashing page serves. The page cannot fetch the image from
# the GitHub release: that URL redirects to a host which sends no CORS header, so
# the browser blocks it. Serving it from this same origin is the only thing that
# works in a browser, and it has to be tracked for Pages to publish it.
#
# This one is published to the whole internet, so it must be the public build --
# the one produced by `tools/validate.sh --prototype`, which compiles with
# AV_PUBLIC_BUILD and therefore never reads main/av_private_config.h. Verified
# for the current file by rebuilding that way with sentinel values in the private
# header: none of them reached the image. Re-verify whenever this file changes;
# publishing a firmware built with the private header would put the WiFi
# credentials and the pairing token on a public web page.
!docs/firmware/FoloToy-AI-Passport-tv.bin

# macOS folder metadata. Written by Finder whenever a directory is opened,
# so it appears without anyone creating it and carries no project content.
.DS_Store
